  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until details of covered, accessible and secure cycle storage enclosure in relation to the storage areas approved under plan reference 5CR(54) Rev A has been submitted to, and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The development shall be carried out in accordance with the details as so agreed, and the storage provision shall be in place prior to the first occupation of the development, and retained thereafter.",
    "Notwithstanding any hereby approved plans and documents, prior to the commencement of the development hereby permitted, a Planning Fire Safety Strategy shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The development shall be carried out and operated in accordance with the approved details in perpetuity.",
    "a) The development shall not be occupied until details of mitigation measures to show how both approved flats will be constructed/adapted so as to provide sufficient air borne and structure borne sound insulation against internally/externally generated noise and vibration (including from the other dwelling and the nearby underground / rail line) has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. This sound insulation shall ensure that the levels of noise generated from the as measured within habitable rooms of the development shall be no higher than 35dB(A)from 7am to 11pm and 30dB(A) in bedrooms from 11pm to 7am.The report shall include all calculations and baseline data, and be set out so that the Local Planning Authority can fully audit the report and critically analyse the content and recommendations.b) The mitigation measures as approved under this condition shall be implemented in their entirety prior to first occupation of the development and retained as such thereafter.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:Site Location Plan; 5CR(51) Rev B – Existing Plans; 5CR(52) Rev B – Existing and Proposed Elevations; 5CR(53) Rev B – Proposed Floor Plans; 5CR(54) Rev A – Existing and Proposed Block Plans; 5CR/HS Design and Access Statement (dated Aug 2024)  All documents received 30.08.24",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved bin storage arrangement under plan reference 5CR(54) Rev A, which shall be in place prior to the first occupation of the development. The refuse and waste bins shall be stored at all times, other than on collection days, within the thereby approved designated refuse storage area",
    "Notwithstanding the hereby approved proposed plans, prior to occupation, both ground floor windows on the east facing side elevation of the property shall be updated to be: (a) of purpose-made obscure glass, (b) be permanently fixed closed below a height of 1.7m above finished floor level, and shall thereafter be retained in that form.Reason - To safeguard the residential amenities of future occupants, in accordance with Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the private outdoor amenity space (and associated boundary fencing) has been provided for both flats, as shown under approved plan reference 5CR(54) Rev A. The development shall operate in accordance with these approved details thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority"
  ],
